{{Navbar-Global Gas Infrastructure Tracker}}
'''Texas Gas Transmission Pipeline''' is an operating natural gas pipeline in the United States.<ref name=source1>[http://bit.ly/2esJPHG Texas Gas Transmission Pipeline,] Wikipedia, accessed January 2018</ref>

==Location==
The pipeline runs from the Louisiana Gulf coast up through Arkansas, Mississippi, Tennessee, and Kentucky, to supply gas to Illinois, Indiana, and Ohio.

==Project Details==

=== Main Line ===
*'''Operator: '''Texas Gas Transmission
*'''Owner: '''Boardwalk Pipeline Partners
*'''Capacity:''' 2800 MMcf/d<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/97452/000009745205000003/tg10k123104.pdf|title=Annual report pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the  Securities Exchange Act of 1934|last=|first=|date=2005|website=Annual report pursuant to section 13 or 15(d) of the  Securities Exchange Act of 1934|url-status=live|archive-url=|archive-date=|access-date=10 August, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/97452/000133604706000012/form10k.htm|title=Annual report pursuant to section 13 or 15(d) of the  Securities Exchange Act of 1934|last=|first=|date=2006|website=United States Securities and Exchange Commission|url-status=live|archive-url=|archive-date=|access-date=10 August, 2023}}</ref>
*'''Length: ''' 5,975 miles<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|url=https://www.txgt.com/about-us/subsidiaries/texas-gas-transmission-llc/default.aspx|title=Boardwalk Pipelines - About Us - Subsidiaries - Texas Gas Transmission, LLC|website=www.txgt.com|language=en-US|access-date=2023-08-10}}</ref>
*'''Diameter:''' 36 inches<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=https://www.offshore-technology.com/marketdata/texas-gas-transmission-gas-pipeline-the-us/|title=Texas Gas Transmission, US|last=|first=|date=29 October, 2021|website=Offshore Technology|url-status=live|archive-url=|archive-date=|access-date=10 August, 2023}}</ref>
*'''Status: '''Operating<ref name=":0" />
*'''Start Year: '''1948<ref name=":1" />

